cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "Faster, cheaper or more accurate? Simulation and economic model of smartphone phenotyping in East African bean breeding"
abstract: >-
  Code and data for a coupled breeding-simulation and economic model that values a
  smartphone computer-vision phenotyping tool in a four-stage East African common-bean
  breeding pipeline. Genetic parameters are estimated from public East African
  multi-environment bean trials. Layer 1 is an AlphaSimR stochastic simulation over a
  factorial grid of tool profiles, with a comparison against the breeder's equation;
  Layer 2 converts simulated genetic gain into adoption, net present value, global
  sensitivity and value-of-information analyses. Includes the variance-component
  analyses, the meta-analysis extraction sheets and the scripts that generate every
  number, table and figure in the manuscript and supplementary material.
